      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We described a 14-year-old boy with initial presentation of recurrent intermittent abdominal pain, with subsequent development of jejunojejunum intussusception. The characteristic purpuric skin rash of Henoch-Schönlein purpura appeared later after the surgical manual reduction. When abdominal pain is the single initial manifestation in patients with undiagnosed Henoch-Schönlein purpura, emergency physicians should evaluate if the patient required early surgical intervention such as intussusception or perforation and always keep Henoch-Schönlein purpura as a possibility in mind."},
